      <title>Results</title>
      <p>Plasma levels reached 10<sup>&#x2212;3</sup> M and the H<sub>2</sub>O content was stable<sup><xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b2">2</xref>,<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b3">3</xref></sup>. Previous work [12] and reviews [3&#x2013;5] agree (<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b4">Smith 2010</xref>; <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b5">Doe 2012</xref>), as summarised in <xref ref-type="table" rid="t1">Table 1</xref> [<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b6">6</xref>].</p>
      <p>The rate law <inline-formula><tex-math>v = \frac{V_{\max} S}{K_m + S}</tex-math></inline-formula> held in all patients.</p>
